# Commit Message Conventions

This project uses [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) enforced by commitlint.

## Format

```
type(scope): short description

optional body with more details
```

## Rules

- **Header max 100 characters**: The first line must be under 100 chars
- **No period at the end**: Don't end the header with a full stop
- **Type is required**: Must start with a valid type
- **Subject is required**: Must have a description after the colon

## Valid Types

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `chore` | Maintenance tasks, dependencies |
| `docs` | Documentation changes |
| `style` | Code style changes (formatting, whitespace) |
| `refactor` | Code refactoring without behavior change |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `build` | Build system or external dependencies |
| `ci` | CI/CD configuration changes |

## Examples

Good:
```
feat: add user authentication flow
fix: resolve memory leak in audio player
chore: update dependencies
docs: add API documentation for media endpoints
refactor: simplify board creation logic
```

Bad:
```
Added new feature.              # No type, ends with period
feat: Add a really long description that goes on and on and exceeds the maximum allowed character limit for commit headers  # Too long
update stuff                    # No type, vague description
```

## Multi-line Commits

For detailed changes, use a body:
```
feat: add audio waveform visualization

Implement real-time waveform display for audio files.
Uses Web Audio API for frequency analysis.
Adds new WaveformCanvas component.
```

## Scopes (Optional)

You can add a scope for more context:
```
feat(auth): add Google OAuth provider
fix(api): handle rate limiting errors
chore(deps): update React to v19
```

## Pre-commit Hooks

This project runs automatically on commit:
- **lint-staged**: Lints and formats staged files
- **commitlint**: Validates commit message format

If your commit is rejected, check the error message and reformat accordingly.
